== Test the semantic driver's diagnostics and emission against clang (part 1 of 8)
# --part deals the driver test's checks (sections, and the cases of its two long sweeps) in turn to 8 parts, one CPU
# each, which the runner packs beside the other commands: alone, the command took 197 s on a hosted runner and 48 s
# on the 9700X, the list's longest. The eight parts together run each check once. As 4 parts, the first was the TSan
# rows' longest command and the x86-64 TSan row's floor (1,287 s on the slowest CPU, #2658's lever 5); part K of 4 is
# parts K and K + 4 of 8, which `costs split` gave each a share of. Buster's runs are this process's, and the oracle
# clang's go to the job's clang server where it built one (#2071); with BUSTER_DRIVER_DIFFERENTIAL, each also runs as
# a child, and a difference fails the command.
"$BUSTER_COMPILER" test-checker-driver --executable "$BUSTER_COMPILER" --part 1/8 --in-process ${BUSTER_CLANG_SERVER:+--clang-server "$BUSTER_CLANG_SERVER"} ${BUSTER_DRIVER_DIFFERENTIAL:+--differential}
